Cell["\<\
Evaluate symham[n] first. The table then connects a symbol such as t1 to a \
definite initial orbital, final orbital, and lattice translation.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c29b0feb-6d97-4379-bfca-54ecdd1925f2"],

Cell["\<\
The two-argument form follows the same parameter through all symmetry-related \
bonds, making it possible to see where every term of the Bloch Hamiltonian \
comes from.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"44df8231-541a-470b-a484-acf8ef412995"],

Cell["\<\
This is an inspection function; it does not solve a missing shell.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"73ed4a61-3bde-4f9c-9677-d073de35806d"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "16a7071c-f509-4714-afe1-cdecd4e7004f"], "\"\<Hermitian\>\"", "True", 
    Cell["\<\
Choose the earlier Hermitian or non-Hermitian shell calculation whose hopping \
origins are to be displayed.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"7bcf0d13-3de7-40c4-95cd-15ae9514099a"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "e6345001-ec55-4cbf-a372-a9f5875fb026"], "\"\<KernelMethod\>\"", \
"\"\<Iterative\>\"", Cell["\<\
Choose the earlier shell calculation made with the \"Iterative\" or \"Stacked\
\" null-space method. A missing calculation is not run automatically.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ae35b3e3-ac13-4b6f-9f19-f850c5e8c43e"]},
